      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَفَازِفُ</span></b>  pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَفْزَفٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  It is also used by a
Hudhalee poet [app. referring to birds] as meaning <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذَوَاتُ زِفَافٍ</span> [i. e., supposing <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زِفَاف</span> to be pl. of
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زِفٌّ</span>, agreeably with analogy, <i>Having small, downy,
feathers</i>]. (TA.)

